{{!--
    ui/env-managed-alert - notice for the settings pages registered through
    lib/ui-routes/settings-page.js, naming the form fields whose values the EENGINE_SETTINGS
    environment variable re-applies on every boot. A value saved for one of them holds only
    until the next restart, and without this the page would show the save succeeding.
    Renders nothing when the page has no such field. The inputs stay enabled on purpose -
    a disabled control drops out of the POST and would silently strip its value from the
    save - so the notice is the whole treatment.
      {{> ui/env-managed-alert}}
    Reads `envManagedKeys` (array of field names) from the page context; registerSettingsPage
    sets it on every render of the page.
--}}
{{#if envManagedKeys.length}}
{{#> ui/alert-banner variant="info" icon="icon-[tabler--info-circle]" title="Some fields are set by the environment"}}
<div>The following settings come from the <code>EENGINE_SETTINGS</code> environment variable and are re-applied on
    every restart. A value saved here is used until the next restart, then reverts to the environment value:
    {{#each envManagedKeys}}<code>{{this}}</code>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.</div>
{{/ui/alert-banner}}
{{/if}}
